Read AGENTS.md. It is the entry point for every agent working on FDOS,
regardless of which tool is driving, and this file deliberately does not
restate it — a second copy would drift, and the drifted copy is the one that
gets read. This file itself was that drifted copy once: it said "there is no
domain code" for three milestones after the domain landed.

Two things before opening anything else:

- The domain code has landed. libs/kernel and libs/ledger exist, and
  libs/contracts is consumed outside this repository at a pinned version. The
  sequencing rule survives that: a new bounded context, canonical type or
  published message still needs the ADR that sequences it first.

- `make verify` is the whole gate. CI runs exactly it (ADR-0014). Never report
  work complete without it passing, and say so plainly if you could not run it.
